{"id":"hj-8","slug":"hj-8","name":"HJ-8","aliases":["Hongjian-8","Red Arrow-8","Hong Jian 8E","Baktar-Shikan","Bakter-Shikan","Baktar Shikan"],"kind":"missile","category":"atgms","subcategory":"Anti-tank missile","description":"The HJ-8 or Hongjian-8 is a second generation tube-launched, optically tracked, wire-guided anti-tank missile system which was originally deployed by the People's Liberation Army in the late 1980s.","development":"In 1970, China's armored corps first proposed to develop a successor to HJ-73 and this was later approved, designated as the AFT-8 or HJ-8. The missile was jointly developed by Research Institute 203 and 282nd Factory, but the program was interrupted by political turmoil. The key designers were Wang Xingzhi (王兴治) and Zhao Jiazheng (赵家铮), who developed the missile. Development was not completed until the early 1980s, after the end of the Cultural Revolution. After receiving state certification, the missile entered mass production in 1984. HJ-8 is an optically tracked, wire guided ATGM.\nHJ-8 and its variants are manufactured by NORINCO's Factory 282 (Jiangnan Machine Factory—江南机器厂), Factory 5618 (Hunan South China Photoelectricity Instrument Plant—湖南华南光电仪器厂) of China and Khan Research Laboratories of Pakistan, now by GIDS.","facts":[],"specifications":[{"group":"Propulsion & Guidance","items":[{"label":"Engine","value":"Solid-fuel rocket"},{"label":"Guidance","value":"SACLOS wire guidance"},{"label":"Launch Platform","value":"Tripod, vehicle, aircraft"}]},{"group":"Dimensions","items":[{"label":"Weight","value":"250 kg","numeric":250,"unit":"kg"},{"label":"Length","value":"1,566 mm","numeric":1566,"unit":"mm"},{"label":"Diameter","value":"120 mm","numeric":120,"unit":"mm"},{"label":"Wingspan","value":"???"}]},{"group":"Performance","items":[{"label":"Operational Range","value":"0.1–4 km"},{"label":"Speed","value":"220 m/s","numeric":220,"unit":"m/s"}]},{"group":"Production","items":[{"label":"Designer","value":"Research Institute 203"},{"label":"Designed","value":"1970–1984"},{"label":"Manufacturer","value":"NORINCO (Factory 282, Factory 5618)"},{"label":"Manufacturer","value":"GIDS (Pakistan)"},{"label":"Produced","value":"1984–present"}]},{"group":"Service","items":[{"label":"Origin","value":"China"},{"label":"In Service","value":"1985–present"}]}],"specIndex":{"Engine":"Solid-fuel rocket","Guidance":"SACLOS wire guidance","Launch Platform":"Tripod, vehicle, aircraft","Weight":"250 kg","Length":"1,566 mm","Diameter":"120 mm","Wingspan":"???","Operational Range":"0.1–4 km","Speed":"220 m/s","Designer":"Research Institute 203","Designed":"1970–1984","Manufacturer":"NORINCO (Factory 282, Factory 5618)","Produced":"1984–present","Origin":"China","In Service":"1985–present"},"images":{"hero":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/40/SLA_Red_Arrow_8L.JPG","width":1600,"height":1200,"license":"See Wikimedia Commons"},"thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/SLA_Red_Arrow_8L.JPG/330px-SLA_Red_Arrow_8L.JPG"},"gallery":[{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c7/Baktar_Shikan_ATGM_in_display_during_2022_MAF%27s_open_day_in_RMAF_Kuantan.jpg","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baktar_Shikan_ATGM_in_display_during_2022_MAF%27s_open_day_in_RMAF_Kuantan.jpg","width":2448,"height":3264,"caption":"Baktar Shikan ATGM in display during 2022 MAF's open day in RMAF Kuantan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","attribution":"Kistara"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f6/ACV_300_Adnan_Baktar_Shikan_ATGM_variant_Kuantan_NDP_2023.jpg","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ACV_300_Adnan_Baktar_Shikan_ATGM_variant_Kuantan_NDP_2023.jpg","width":2566,"height":1903,"caption":"ACV 300 Adnan Baktar Shikan ATGM variant Kuantan NDP 2023","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","attribution":"Kistara"},{"